    "review::.::holistic::naming_quality::diagnostics_screen_name_collision": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::naming_quality::diagnostics_screen_name_collision",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "showDiagnosticsScreen() and uiShowDiagnostics() are near-identically named but have different blocking behavior",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "naming_quality",
        "related_files": [
          "src/ui/diagnostics.h",
          "src/ui/diagnostics.cpp",
          "src/ui/display_ui.h",
          "src/main.cpp"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "src/ui/diagnostics.cpp: showDiagnosticsScreen() calls uiShowDiagnostics(...) then uiWaitForTap() internally \u2014 it draws AND blocks.",
          "src/ui/display_ui.h: uiShowDiagnostics(...) only draws; every other screen (uiShowBenchmarkResult, uiShowSpiScaleResult) is explicitly followed by a separate uiWaitForTap() call in main.cpp, so the caller controls blocking everywhere except diagnostics.",
          "src/main.cpp: case HomeAction::Diagnostics calls showDiagnosticsScreen() alone (no visible uiWaitForTap()), while case HomeAction::BenchmarkMenu's inner loop calls uiShowBenchmarkResult(...) followed by an explicit uiWaitForTap() \u2014 the same blocking effect is spelled two different ways depending on which near-identical name you use."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Rename the orchestrator to make the blocking behavior explicit and visually distinct from the ui* draw-only family, e.g. runDiagnosticsScreen() or showDiagnosticsAndWait(), so it can't be confused with uiShowDiagnostics() at a glance.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "3d1095d6"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Batch 3/3: resolved the showDiagnosticsScreen()/uiShowDiagnostics() naming collision by inlining the wrapper into main.cpp as showDiagnostics() (see the abstraction_fitness fix); renamed printCardIdentity() to printCardReport() to match its actual scope; moved card_format.*/card_identity.*/touch_calibration.* from util/ into hardware/ (their only consumers), eliminating the util/ directory entirely; added .github/workflows/native-tests.yml running 'pio test -e native' on push/PR; rewrote CLAUDE.md's Build commands section to document the real env:native Unity suite and its six covered modules; moved fsName() into hardware/sd_card.cpp using SdFat's FAT_TYPE_FAT12/16/32/EXFAT constants instead of raw literals (same reasoning as cardTypeName()); changed the one stray static_cast in card_format.cpp to a C-style cast to match the codebase's universal convention.",
