    "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::sd_scan_result_shape_asymmetry": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::sd_scan_result_shape_asymmetry",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "scanCard() and runSpiScalingBenchmark() expose per-attempt SPI results through different API shapes",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "api_surface_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "src/hardware/sd_card.h",
          "src/hardware/sd_card.cpp",
          "src/benchmark/benchmark.h",
          "src/benchmark/spi_scale_benchmark.cpp",
          "src/core/app_types.h"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "sd_card.h: bool scanCard() returns only success/failure; per-speed detail (AttemptResult{hz, stage, errorCode, errorData}) is only reachable afterward via the separate globals getAttempts()/getAttemptCount().",
          "benchmark.h: SpiScaleResult runSpiScalingBenchmark() returns a self-contained struct whose SpiScalePoint{hz, ok, rawReadMBs, efficiencyPercent, errorCode, errorData} entries carry the same kind of per-attempt outcome directly in the return value -- no separate getter needed.",
          "Both functions iterate the same kind of 'try each SPI speed, record stage/errorCode/errorData' loop (sd_card.cpp scanCard() vs spi_scale_benchmark.cpp runSpiScalingBenchmark()), so a caller familiar with one would reasonably but incorrectly assume the other follows the same access pattern."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Make scanCard() return the same kind of self-contained result the scaling benchmark uses -- e.g. have it populate and return (or take a reference to) an array/struct of AttemptResult directly, instead of requiring a follow-up getAttempts()/getAttemptCount() call. This removes the global-state readout path without adding any new abstraction.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "b502e40a"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Batch 1/3 of review-finding fixes: inlined diagnostics.cpp's single-caller glue into main.cpp (matching rescan()/runBenchMenu()); extracted shared recordSdError() into hardware/sd_card.h/.cpp; removed unconditional debug Serial.printf calls from touch.cpp's readTouch(); documented the scanCard()-vs-runSpiScalingBenchmark() return-shape difference as intentional (persistent queryable state vs one-shot result) in sd_card.h; documented runSpiScalingBenchmark()'s rescan side effect on its declaration in benchmark.h; changed touch_calibration.cpp's anonymous namespace to static (matching codebase convention); reformatted touch.h/touch.cpp from compact to the dominant one-arg-per-line style; pinned TFT_eSPI@2.5.43 and SdFat@2.3.1 in platformio.ini; extracted a shared runChunkedIo() helper replacing the triplicated write/read/verify loops in benchmark.cpp; extracted printBenchmarkResult() out of runQuickBenchmark().",
