    "review::.::holistic::package_organization::util_dir_hardware_affinity_mismatch": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::package_organization::util_dir_hardware_affinity_mismatch",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "util/ holds hardware-only helpers (card_format, card_identity, touch_calibration) while equally pure bench_math/ui_geometry stay in their own domain folders",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "package_organization",
        "related_files": [
          "src/util/card_format.h",
          "src/util/card_identity.h",
          "src/util/touch_calibration.h",
          "src/hardware/sd_card.h",
          "src/hardware/touch.cpp",
          "src/benchmark/bench_math.h",
          "src/ui/ui_geometry.h"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "card_format.h and card_identity.h are included solely by src/hardware/sd_card.h; touch_calibration.h is included solely by src/hardware/touch.cpp -- each is 100% single-domain, not shared across hardware/, benchmark/, and ui/.",
          "bench_math.h ('Pure benchmark math -- no hardware/Arduino dependency, safe to unit-test on host, see test/test_bench_math') and ui_geometry.h ('Pure UI geometry math -- no TFT_eSPI/Arduino dependency, safe to unit-test on host, see test/test_ui_geometry') use the exact same justification as the util/ files but were left inside benchmark/ and ui/ respectively.",
          "directory_profiles: util/ imported_by_dirs = {hardware: 3, tests: 3} -- confirms util/'s three production files exist purely for hardware/, not as a genuine cross-cutting layer."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Pick one consistent rule and apply it to all five pure/testable modules. Simplest: fold the single-consumer pure helpers back into their owning domain (matches the pattern already used for bench_math and ui_geometry, and needs no new directory). Staged plan: (1) git mv src/util/card_format.h src/util/card_format.cpp src/hardware/ and in src/hardware/sd_card.h change '#include \"../util/card_format.h\"' to '#include \"card_format.h\"'; (2) git mv src/util/card_identity.h src/util/card_identity.cpp src/hardware/ and update the matching include in sd_card.h the same way; (3) git mv src/util/touch_calibration.h src/util/touch_calibration.cpp src/hardware/ and update '#include \"../util/touch_calibration.h\"' to '#include \"touch_calibration.h\"' in src/hardware/touch.cpp; (4) update the three include paths in test/test_card_format/test_card_format.cpp, test/test_card_identity/test_card_identity.cpp, test/test_touch_calibration/test_touch_calibration.cpp from '../../src/util/...' to '../../src/hardware/...'; (5) delete the now-empty src/util/ directory; (6) validate with `pio run` (firmware build) and the native/host test environment (e.g. `pio test -e native`) to confirm both the device build and the host-run pure-logic tests still pass.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "d665966f"
