    "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::sd_state_restore_by_convention": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::sd_state_restore_by_convention",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "SPI-scaling benchmark leaves shared SdFs singleton in a scaled state unless its trailing scanCard() call is preserved",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "initialization_coupling",
        "related_files": [
          "src/benchmark/spi_scale_benchmark.cpp",
          "src/hardware/sd_card.cpp"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "runSpiScalingBenchmark() in spi_scale_benchmark.cpp calls sd.end()/sd.cardBegin() at several SPI speeds, then relies on a final scanCard() call (with only a comment explaining why) to put the shared sd/info singleton back into its normal qualified state.",
          "Any future caller that touches the SdFs singleton directly (bypassing scanCard()) between scaling passes, or a future edit that removes/reorders the trailing scanCard() call, would leave getCardInfo()/getSd() reflecting a stale scaled-speed state with no compiler or runtime check to catch it."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Keep the fix local and simple: rename scanCard()'s role at the end of runSpiScalingBenchmark() to make the restoration explicit at the call site (e.g. a one-line comment already exists; strengthen it by asserting info.cardOk after the restore call, or return a bool from runSpiScalingBenchmark() reflecting whether restore succeeded) rather than introducing a new abstraction layer or session/guard object.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "f5d0e413"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Batch 2/3: moved allocateDmaBuffer() into hardware/sd_card.h/.cpp so sd_card.cpp and benchmark_raw.cpp share one implementation instead of duplicating it; added CardInfo::volumeErrorCode/volumeErrorData, populated via recordSdError() on sd.volumeBegin() failure; moved uiWaitForTap()'s definition into display_ui_internal.cpp next to header()/lineRow(); added a sd.card() null check at the top of rawReadAtCurrentSpeed(); strengthened the scanCard()-restores-state doc comment on runSpiScalingBenchmark() in benchmark.h; extracted runChunkedIo() to remove the timedFileWrite/timedFileRead/verifyFile triplication; split uiShowSpiScaleResult() into scaleGraphMaxSpeed()/drawScaleGraphFrame()/scalePointCoords()/drawScalePoint()/buildScaleSummary() helpers; reformatted touch.cpp and tightened bench_math.cpp's one compact expression to the dominant vertical style; documented runSpiScalingBenchmark()'s hidden rescan on its declaration in benchmark.h; added explicit '../hardware/card_format.h' and '../hardware/card_identity.h' includes to every ui/ and benchmark/ file that calls those functions, instead of relying on sd_card.h's transitive include.",
      "first_seen": "2026-09-22T11:43:45+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-09-22T11:43:45+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-09-22T15:08:15+00:00",
