    "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::benchmark_calls_ui_directly": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::benchmark_calls_ui_directly",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "benchmark.cpp's runChunkedIo() calls uiShowProgress() directly, coupling the benchmark logic layer to the ui presentation layer",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "cross_module_architecture",
        "related_files": [
          "src/benchmark/benchmark.cpp",
          "src/ui/display_ui.h"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "src/benchmark/benchmark.cpp:9 includes \"../ui/display_ui.h\", and runChunkedIo() calls uiShowProgress(title, stage, done, BENCH_TEST_SIZE, ...) at lines 98, 139 (plus two more call sites later in the file at ~361/429) to render live progress mid-loop",
          "src/benchmark/benchmark_internal.h states the project's own rule for this direction one file over: 'hardware/ can't depend back on benchmark/' -- the same reasoning (lower layers must not depend on higher/sibling layers) is violated here by benchmark depending on ui",
          "Sibling files spi_scale_benchmark.cpp and benchmark_raw.cpp implement the other two benchmark passes without any ui/ include, so this is not a subsystem-wide pattern but a one-off in a single file"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Have runChunkedIo() accept a simple function-pointer/lambda progress callback (matching the existing ChunkIoFn pattern already used in the same file for chunkWrite/chunkRead/chunkReadAndCrc) that main.cpp or benchmark.cpp's caller wires to uiShowProgress, instead of benchmark.cpp including ui/display_ui.h directly. This keeps benchmark/ dependent only on core/ and hardware/, matching the rule already documented in benchmark_internal.h, without introducing a heavier abstraction than the codebase already uses elsewhere.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "2acf45ae"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Documented runQuickBenchmark()'s no-side-effect/default-result contract in benchmark.h; surfaced BenchmarkResult.cleanupOk in printBenchmarkResult and removed dead CardInfo::csdOk (with its test assertion); confirmed identityCheckName()/header() defs already matched their headers (stale finding from before a mid-review fix landed); split makeSdConfig(uint32_t hz) in sd_card.h/.cpp to one-arg-per-line (the remaining compact holdout); added a BenchmarkProgressFn callback threaded through runChunkedIo()/timedFileWrite/timedFileRead/verifyFile/runQuickBenchmark so benchmark.cpp no longer includes ui/display_ui.h, with main.cpp passing uiShowProgress as the callback; added CardInfo-style ioErrorCode/ioErrorData to BenchmarkResult, populated via recordSdError() on any chunk-transfer failure and on sd.open() failure, and printed in printBenchmarkResult(); switched rawReadAtCurrentSpeed() to call the shared recordSdError() with a formatted 'RAW READ LBA %lu' label instead of its own inline Serial.printf; updated CLAUDE.md's Architecture section to describe main.cpp's inlined showDiagnostics() instead of the removed diagnostics.* module; removed the unused RAW_TEST_SECTORS constant from config.h; renamed touch.h/touch.cpp's readTouch() sx/sy params to screenX/screenY matching mapTouchToScreen()'s naming; moved scaleGraphMaxSpeed()/scalePointCoords()/buildScaleSummary() from display_results.cpp into ui_geometry.h/.cpp (now in the native test_build_src_filter) with 9 new Unity tests covering edge cases (single-point graphs, failed/zero-speed points, first-successful-point summary); retyped ChunkIoFn's void* context to a concrete uint32_t* crcAccum since only chunkReadAndCrc ever used it.",
      "first_seen": "2026-09-22T15:35:35+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-09-22T15:35:35+00:00",
