          "touch.cpp's readTouch() computes fully-spelled `rawX`/`rawY` locals, then passes them to `mapTouchToScreen(rawX, rawY, sx, sy)` - mixing descriptive and abbreviated names for coordinate values within the same function.",
          "touch_calibration.h's mapTouchToScreen() uses `int& screenX, int& screenY` for the identical output concept, and ui_geometry.h uses `pointX`/`pointY`/`rectX`/`rectY` for coordinates elsewhere - sx/sy is the only abbreviated pair in the codebase's coordinate-naming vocabulary."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Rename readTouch()'s `sx`/`sy` parameters to `screenX`/`screenY` in both touch.h and touch.cpp (and update the two call sites in main.cpp's parameter names only if desired - the call sites already use local `x`/`y`, which is fine) so the same concept is spelled the same way everywhere it appears.",
