    "review::.::holistic::test_strategy::untested_pure_logic_in_display_results": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::test_strategy::untested_pure_logic_in_display_results",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Pure SPI-scale-graph math in display_results.cpp has zero test coverage despite having no hardware dependency",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "test_strategy",
        "related_files": [
          "src/ui/display_results.cpp",
          "src/ui/ui_geometry.h",
          "platformio.ini"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "scaleGraphMaxSpeed(), scalePointCoords(), and buildScaleSummary() in src/ui/display_results.cpp perform only float/int arithmetic and snprintf formatting -- none call tft() or any TFT_eSPI API -- yet the file is not in platformio.ini's env:native build_src_filter, so these functions only ever run on real hardware.",
          "The same category of logic (hitTestRect, computeBarFillWidth) already lives in src/ui/ui_geometry.cpp specifically so it can be host-tested (test/test_ui_geometry/test_ui_geometry.cpp), so this is an inconsistent application of the codebase's own established pattern rather than a novel gap.",
          "scalePointCoords() has non-trivial edge-case behavior worth locking down (count==1 divide-by-max(1,count-1), point.ok==false vs maxSpeed<=0.0f branches) that is currently unverified by any test."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Move scaleGraphMaxSpeed(), scalePointCoords(), and buildScaleSummary() into ui_geometry.h/.cpp (they take only primitives/SpiScaleResult, which is already hardware-free), add ui_geometry.cpp's existing env:native filter entry (no platformio.ini change needed since it's already included), and add Unity tests mirroring test_ui_geometry.cpp's style: count==1, no successful point (summary stays empty), and a failed point sitting at the graph floor.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "c7cce9b8"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Documented runQuickBenchmark()'s no-side-effect/default-result contract in benchmark.h; surfaced BenchmarkResult.cleanupOk in printBenchmarkResult and removed dead CardInfo::csdOk (with its test assertion); confirmed identityCheckName()/header() defs already matched their headers (stale finding from before a mid-review fix landed); split makeSdConfig(uint32_t hz) in sd_card.h/.cpp to one-arg-per-line (the remaining compact holdout); added a BenchmarkProgressFn callback threaded through runChunkedIo()/timedFileWrite/timedFileRead/verifyFile/runQuickBenchmark so benchmark.cpp no longer includes ui/display_ui.h, with main.cpp passing uiShowProgress as the callback; added CardInfo-style ioErrorCode/ioErrorData to BenchmarkResult, populated via recordSdError() on any chunk-transfer failure and on sd.open() failure, and printed in printBenchmarkResult(); switched rawReadAtCurrentSpeed() to call the shared recordSdError() with a formatted 'RAW READ LBA %lu' label instead of its own inline Serial.printf; updated CLAUDE.md's Architecture section to describe main.cpp's inlined showDiagnostics() instead of the removed diagnostics.* module; removed the unused RAW_TEST_SECTORS constant from config.h; renamed touch.h/touch.cpp's readTouch() sx/sy params to screenX/screenY matching mapTouchToScreen()'s naming; moved scaleGraphMaxSpeed()/scalePointCoords()/buildScaleSummary() from display_results.cpp into ui_geometry.h/.cpp (now in the native test_build_src_filter) with 9 new Unity tests covering edge cases (single-point graphs, failed/zero-speed points, first-successful-point summary); retyped ChunkIoFn's void* context to a concrete uint32_t* crcAccum since only chunkReadAndCrc ever used it.",
      "first_seen": "2026-09-22T15:35:35+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-09-22T15:35:35+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-09-22T15:41:01+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "work_item_kind": "review_defect",
      "issue_kind": "review_defect",
