        "evidence": [
          "app_types.h: BenchmarkResult declares preallocOk/fileWriteOk/fileReadOk/verifyOk/rawReadOk defaulting to false but cleanupOk defaulting to true -- the only field with 'succeeded unless proven otherwise' semantics in the struct.",
          "benchmark.cpp sets result.cleanupOk once (line ~437); no file in src/ui or src/benchmark reads it afterward (printBenchmarkResult() and uiShowBenchmarkResult() both skip it).",
          "sd_card.cpp's fillCardIdentity() sets info.csdOk = true alongside info.cidOk = true, but only cidOk is later read (by identityCheckName()); csdOk has no reader anywhere in src/."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Either surface these fields where the other *Ok fields already surface (e.g. show cleanup status in printBenchmarkResult()'s Serial summary, or fold csdOk into identityCheckName()'s check alongside cidOk), or remove the fields if they don't need to be tracked -- don't leave declared-but-unconsumed status fields in a struct whose sibling fields are all consumed.",
