    "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::raw_read_failure_no_error_code": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::raw_read_failure_no_error_code",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "runQuickBenchmark() captures no SD error code when the raw sector read fails, unlike its open/write/read/verify failure paths",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "src/benchmark/benchmark.cpp",
          "src/benchmark/benchmark_raw.cpp",
          "src/benchmark/spi_scale_benchmark.cpp"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "benchmark.cpp:499-504: `result.rawReadOk = rawReadAtCurrentSpeed(buffer, BENCH_TEST_SIZE, result.rawReadMBs);` passes no error out-params, while the open/write/read/verify paths just above it (lines 443-487) all thread `result.ioErrorCode`/`result.ioErrorData` through.",
          "benchmark_raw.cpp:66-84: rawReadAtCurrentSpeed() does call recordSdError() on failure, but stores the code/data into local stack variables that go out of scope on return \u2014 the caller never sees them.",
          "spi_scale_benchmark.cpp:94-105 shows the pattern that would close this gap: after rawReadAtCurrentSpeed() fails there, it calls recordSdError(sd, point.errorCode, point.errorData, \"BENCH\") a second time to capture the code into its own result struct.",
          "printBenchmarkResult() (benchmark.cpp:346-353) only prints the 'I/O error: XX/XX' line when ioErrorCode||ioErrorData is nonzero, so a raw-read failure shows only the generic 'Raw read: FAILED' with no code, unlike every other I/O failure surfaced in the same report."
        ],
        "suggestion": "In runQuickBenchmark(), immediately after the rawReadAtCurrentSpeed() call, if !result.rawReadOk call recordSdError(sd, result.ioErrorCode, result.ioErrorData, \"RAW READ\") \u2014 mirroring exactly what spi_scale_benchmark.cpp already does at its own rawReadAtCurrentSpeed() call site. No signature change needed since the SD error state is still valid immediately after the failed call returns.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "5e71e32f"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Reformatted cardTypeName()/fsName() (sd_card.cpp) and attemptStageName()/resolveVendor() (card_identity.cpp) definitions to one-arg-per-line, matching their own headers and the codebase convention; added a recordSdError() call in runQuickBenchmark() after a raw-read failure, populating result.ioErrorCode/ioErrorData (mirroring spi_scale_benchmark.cpp's existing pattern for the same call); surfaced CardInfo.volumeErrorCode/volumeErrorData via a new 'mount error: XX/XX' line in printCardReport() when the volume fails to mount.",
