    "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::benchmark_prealloc_seekset_no_error_capture": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::benchmark_prealloc_seekset_no_error_capture",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "runQuickBenchmark() captures no SD error code on preAllocate()/seekSet() failure, unlike every other I/O failure branch in the same function",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "src/benchmark/benchmark.cpp"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "file.preAllocate(BENCH_TEST_SIZE) failure only prints a local Serial.printf PASS/FAIL line and sets result.preallocOk=false -- no recordSdError() call.",
          "The three 'if (... && file.seekSet(0))' guards silently fall through to leaving fileWriteOk/fileReadOk/verifyOk false with no error capture, while every other failure branch in this same function (chunk transfer, sd.open(), raw read) does call recordSdError() to populate result.ioErrorCode/ioErrorData."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Call recordSdError(sd, result.ioErrorCode, result.ioErrorData, \"PREALLOC\") when preAllocate() fails, and a similar call (e.g. \"SEEK\") when any of the three file.seekSet(0) calls fail, mirroring the existing pattern used for every other failure branch in runQuickBenchmark().",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "9b563ed3"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Extracted the prealloc/seek/write/read/seek/verify sequence in runQuickBenchmark() into a new runFileBenchmarkSequence() helper (benchmark.cpp) using early returns, with recordSdError() called on every failing step (preallocate, each seekSet, and the timed steps which already recorded internally) -- this both closes the missing-error-capture gap and reads more clearly than the prior nested if/else chain. Gave rawReadAtCurrentSpeed() proper uint8_t& errorCode/errorData out-params (benchmark_raw.cpp + benchmark_internal.h) instead of discarding its precise per-LBA recordSdError() result into unused locals; both call sites (runQuickBenchmark in benchmark.cpp, runSpiScalingBenchmark in spi_scale_benchmark.cpp) now receive that error directly instead of redundantly re-deriving a coarser one. Made ui_geometry.cpp's buildScaleSummary() fall back to showing the first attempted point's SD error code when no speed qualified, instead of leaving the SPI-scale summary line blank -- so SpiScalePoint.errorCode/errorData are now genuinely read and displayed, with 2 new Unity tests covering the fallback and empty-result cases.",
      "first_seen": "2026-09-22T20:11:42+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-09-22T20:11:42+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-09-22T20:12:09+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "work_item_kind": "review_defect",
      "issue_kind": "review_defect",
      "origin": "review_import",
      "lang": "cxx",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null,
      "resolution_attestation": {
        "kind": "manual",
