    "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::raw_read_error_discarded_then_reconstructed": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::raw_read_error_discarded_then_reconstructed",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "rawReadAtCurrentSpeed() computes a precise per-LBA SD error internally but discards it, forcing both callers to redundantly re-derive a coarser version",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "src/benchmark/benchmark_raw.cpp",
          "src/benchmark/benchmark.cpp",
          "src/benchmark/spi_scale_benchmark.cpp"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "benchmark_raw.cpp: recordSdError() is called into local 'uint8_t errorCode; uint8_t errorData;' that are immediately discarded when the function returns false -- rawReadAtCurrentSpeed()'s signature (benchmark_internal.h) has no error out-params, unlike sibling chunked-I/O helpers timedFileWrite/timedFileRead/verifyFile which all take 'uint8_t& errorCode, uint8_t& errorData'.",
          "benchmark.cpp's runQuickBenchmark() and spi_scale_benchmark.cpp's runSpiScalingBenchmark() both re-call recordSdError() themselves right after rawReadAtCurrentSpeed() returns false, relying on sd's error state being unchanged since the internal call, and using a generic 'RAW READ'/'BENCH' label instead of the internal call's precise 'RAW READ LBA %lu' label -- so the more useful diagnostic (which sector failed) never reaches the persisted result, only a transient Serial line."
